Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] F635-2: the evolved Mega Knight uppercut row's own
 GameTagsToSet (data 16.635.3)

A row that sets its tags (NO_ATTACK, NO_MOVE_ALLOW_ATTRACT) holds the unit with them while its run is listed,
in place of the coded NO_ATTACK and NO_MOVE; LOCK_TARGET at the push stays coded. Inferred from the tables
(the same update turned the root's NO_MOVE into NO_MOVE_ALLOW_ATTRACT); the 7 recorded matches diverge
before it shows, coded and row hold alike (b).
Core tests: 16.402.22 2143/0; 16.635.3 (guard bypassed for the run) 28 -> 16 failures. Three tests read the
hold from the row: anUppercutOnATowerEndsAtOnce, aPushOnANoPushbackTargetIsRefused; the held-dasher scene
takes the row's tags off to keep its NO_MOVE hold.
